{
  "_comment": "Claude Code Pack TASTE - safety baseline for the TASTE ambassador / power-user cohort. The deny rules, the bash-safety-extended.py hook, and disableBypassPermissionsMode are the safety net. The allow list mirrors a trusted power-user setup so day-to-day work (read-only inspection, build tools, media tooling, git) does not nag; install-class, network-reaching, and destructive commands stay in ask/deny. Cost guardrails are intentionally NOT enforced - the team plan ceiling is per-seat and people work fast; hard caps would block real work. Tighten or loosen per project in settings.local.json as you learn what you trust.",
